daqp-fortran is a modern Fortran port of DAQP, a dual active-set solver for
dense convex quadratic programs, by Daniel Arnström:

    https://github.com/darnstrom/daqp (MIT licence)

The port follows DAQP v0.10.3 (commit 29a8987d8b9a596c1ab6acf84c17d38b068b73bc).
The files src/daqp_core.f90 and src/daqp_module.f90 are translations of, and
changes to, DAQP's C sources (src/*.c and include/*.h of that repository).

The method is described in:

    D. Arnström, A. Bemporad, D. Axehill, "A dual active-set solver for
    embedded quadratic programming using recursive LDL^T updates", IEEE
    Transactions on Automatic Control 67(8), 4362-4369, 2022.

The directory upstream/daqp is a git submodule holding DAQP's own repository,
under its own licence. It is not part of this package's sources: fpm does not
build it. It is only used to compare the port with the original (compare/).
